WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
 Would Dr. Zane, Dr. Khoury please. Dr. Nizar Zane is going to induct Dr. Wael

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:07.000
 Khoury.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.610
 Dr. Nizar Zane is the chairman and medical director of his global patient

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.000
 services at Cleveland Clinic.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.810
 He's the chief of hepatology and medical director of liver transplantation at

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.000
 Cleveland Clinic.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.250
 He's also well known for his academic achievements, his active inmates at the

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.000
 local, national and international levels.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
 Dr. Nizar Zane will induct Dr. Wael Khoury.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:39.000
 Thank you for the kind invitation to do this presentation.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.920
 With all the strength and wisdom of Wael, I think he made a mistake by choosing

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.000
 me to do this presentation.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.570
 But in fact, to be truthful, on Saturday I spent almost an entire day trying to

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:57.000
 write remarks.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.380
 I tried to think of Wael and since I met him, what I know about him, what he

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:02.000
 had done.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.240
 And it ended up being probably seven or eight pages and then I had to cut it

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.000
 down.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.000
 So he is a very accomplished person.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.630
 So it is very humbling and a great honor to introduce someone I have admired

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.000
 for so many years.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:23.000
 And I hope he was inspired to reach the standards he set and achieved himself.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.000
 For that I thank you all.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.000
 He is un-exordinally outstanding and outstanding in many ways.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:37.640
 Dr. Khoury is blessed with an enormous self-confidence that had its roots in

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:44.000
 his knowledge, skills and in his great intellectual capabilities.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:50.390
 His mind has sort of unshaken with voice and serenity that helped him remain

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:53.000
 unfilled and true to his principles.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:01.080
 As he represented and passionately defended the values of a structured woman

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:06.000
 and a divided Syrian American society.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.200
 At his level of honesty, elegance and cultural refinement, he was above those

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.000
 strategies.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:20.090
 Dr. Wael Khoury was and continues to be the glue of our local diverse Arab

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:24.000
 American society here in Cleveland.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:30.000
 It was once said that the apen does not fall far from the tree.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:38.000
 Dr. Wael Khoury and his father are undoubtedly made from the same cloth.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:45.800
 The late Mr. Shahada Khoury is an intellectual icon in Syria and across the

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.000
 Arab world.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:53.690
 He was a leader in modernizing Arabic language for its use in contemporary

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.000
 sciences.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:02.000
 Clearly Wael was heavily and positively influenced by his father's passion for

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.000
 knowledge and acquired many of his leadership skills.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:13.340
 As a distinguished member of the local medical community for many years, Dr. Khoury

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:17.000
 served as the President of Cardiology Associates of Cleveland

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:25.090
 and as the Head of Cardiology at Merriman Hospital for over 130 consecutive

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:26.000
 years.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.980
 He was appointed as the Chief of Staff at Merriman between 1993 and 1995 and as

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:39.000
 the Vice President for Medical Affairs between 1995 and 2001.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:46.160
 Arguably, one of his best accomplishments during these years was his successful

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:53.560
 petitioning at the state level for hospitals with less than 250 dead capacity

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:58.000
 to have cardiac catheterization facilities.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:04.150
 This achievement saved many lives when patients did not have the luxury of time

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:08.000
 to be transferred to larger medical centers.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.000
 But that's not why we are here tonight.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:15.780
 We are here tonight to acknowledge the many contributions of the man with an

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.000
 inherent and true passion for public service.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:25.040
 Dr. Wael Khoury embodies all the values of public servants working for the

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.000
 common good for social progress and equality.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:34.720
 It was his passion for public service that led Dr. Khoury nearly 20 years ago

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:40.000
 to join the Cleveland Council on the Board of Affairs at CCWA.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.000
 With whom he shared a vision and a mission.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:49.520
 Soon he became a member of the board at CCWA and ever since has actively worked

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:52.000
 to promote the Council's mission.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.990
 That is to inspire engagement in international affairs and work culture through

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:02.000
 education, public dialogue and citizen diplomacy.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:09.440
 Wael served as the Chairman of the Board of CCWA between 2012 and 2015 and

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:15.000
 resumed his position again in 2016.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:20.610
 As a Chairman, Wael never sees to us how the Council can reach out to more

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:24.000
 Clevelanders, especially the youth.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:30.930
 CCWA's modern United Nations program now brings nearly 54 schools and 1,800

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.000
 students.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.880
 Dr. Wael Khoury also put his heart and soul into ensuring that Cleveland gains

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:44.000
 an awareness and benefits of serious rich and colorful culture.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:49.710
 Thus he became the founding President of the Syrian American Cultural Council

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.000
 in 2005.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:57.170
 Out of that we never knew the vision of having a Syrian garden among Cleveland's

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:02.000
 great cultural gardens along Martin Luther King Boulevard.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:09.050
 Wael saw his dream fulfilled in September of 2015 with the official

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:15.360
 inauguration of the Unmagnificent Syrian Garden, a worthy tribute to the deep

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.000
 history and culture of Syria.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:23.070
 Recently, thanks to his time as commitment to the concept of cultural gardens

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:28.620
 Dr. Khoury was elected to be the President of the Executive Board of the

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:32.000
 Cleveland Cultural Gardens Federation.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:38.000
 In fact, I believe he started his role this month or last month.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:44.990
 As we celebrate the accomplishments of Wael, it would quantity a half-finished

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:51.850
 presentation without speaking of the woman besides him, who will not met you

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:53.000
 but with Wael.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:07:13.680
 I don't know how that makes me feel. His wife Sousa, and I talked with Sousa,

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.000
 and I talked with Speed and Earth on her own.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:21.220
 Not only is it a symbol of elegance and class, Sousa, the inspiration and the

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:27.000
 energy that keeps Wael enthusiastically working on his many projects.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:33.110
 This is apparent to all of us who were privileged to spend a lot of time with

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:35.000
 the Khoury family.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:41.250
 Sousa is an educator by profession and a dedicated civic leader promoting our

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:47.600
 city through her own work with the Cleveland Film Festival among several other

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:50.000
 societies and foundations.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:59.910
 Sousa also ensures that Wael is up and working all night long. This may be

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:03.000
 interpreted in many different ways.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:09.490
 But what I meant by it is that if you know Wael, Khoury, you always receive

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:13.000
 emails from Wael between 2 and 5 AM.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:18.000
 And you can't help but wonder what this man ever sees.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:24.000
 In fact, at night between 2 and 5 AM, there are only two types of communication.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:29.000
 Tweets from President Trump's and emails from Trump's.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:37.000
 So we said earlier that the apple does not fall far from the tree.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:42.210
 The legacy of Wael would undoubtedly continue into the next generation of Khoury

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:43.000
 family.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:48.220
 Sousa and Wael are less than four lovely and equally as accomplished children,

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:54.400
 not only achievers by every academic standard, but filled with their parents'

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:59.460
 aspirations for civil and community service and for the honorable purpose of

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:02.000
 bridging acts among culture.

